; membrane-lane-live.fk — the membrane observer made bidirectional: owed crossings become live asks.
;
; membrane-lane.fk READS a lane (which crossings left the body, which are still owed a re-witness). This
; cell turns that read into the loop AGENTS.md item 8 requires: each owed crossing is emitted as an outbound
; observation AND a correlated inbound control — request-evidence (action 4) — on the body's own bidirectional
; framebuffer channel, and when a re-witness lands (ml-close) the debt shrinks on re-observe. Observation flows
; out, a correlated control flows back, the state is re-observed. A membrane crossing is no longer a passive
; note; it is an open question the body actually asks.
;
; The honest shape of the ask: request-evidence does NOT change the answer. bfc-apply returns the current
; state for a request-evidence control (only rehearse-ground, action 5, swaps in the rehearsed state), and it
; returns the explicit ALTERNATIVE when no response arrives — never silence. So an owed crossing asks for its
; evidence, holds the state while it waits, and falls to a named alternative if nothing comes. Evidence is
; requested, never fabricated; that is the whole discipline.
;
; twinblind: the correlation (exchange-id = crossing id), the count (one ask per owed crossing), and the
; apply outcomes are CANONICAL — one right answer, no oracle. A self-check is a real falsifier.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk observe/membrane-lane.fk observe/bidirectional-framebuffer-channel.fk
;
; Proven by: observe/tests/membrane-lane-live-band.fk (verdict 31).

(do
    ; one owed crossing -> an outbound observation. exchange-id IS the crossing id, so the
    ; response can be correlated back to exactly the crossing it addresses. The alternative
    ; (the no-response fallback) is the crossing id: with no evidence, we re-ask about it.
    (defn mll-observe (c) (bfc-envelope 0 (ml-id c) 0 c (ml-id c)))
    ; the correlated control: request evidence (action 4) for that owed crossing.
    (defn mll-request (c) (bfc-control (mll-observe c) 4))

    ; over a lane: one (observation . request) pair per OWED crossing. A native lane owes
    ; nothing, so it asks nothing — the sovereign lane needs no evidence.
    (defn mll-pairs-loop (owed)
        (if (eq (len owed) 0) (empty)
            (cons (list (mll-observe (head owed)) (mll-request (head owed)))
                  (mll-pairs-loop (tail owed)))))
    (defn mll-pairs (lane) (mll-pairs-loop (ml-owed-list lane)))
    (defn mll-request-count (lane) (len (mll-pairs lane)))

    ; accessors into a pair
    (defn mll-pair-obs (p) (nth p 0))
    (defn mll-pair-req (p) (nth p 1))

    ; the re-observe half: apply an owed crossing's ask against an inbound response.
    ; request-evidence holds the current state (the ask is logged, the answer is not
    ; touched); no/ mismatched response selects the named alternative, never silence.
    (defn mll-apply (c inbound current rehearsed)
        (bfc-apply (mll-observe c) inbound current rehearsed))
    0)
